{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact local NF-5 head b8d58825fed6475718761771096f6f7e8b644b8f, tree 5ad88394b9dfc03ec2be385239ffff63d58900e9, on builder/nf5-on-c2-main-20261114, all 46 artifacts, for request c80d0424 under implementation promise 11ad3b37 and my promise filed for this request. I read the head from the shared object store. The branch is not on origin. NF-5 moves the browser's requests into `Custody` with an IndexedDB store, deletes `request-custody.ts`, `request-attempts.ts` and `request-dispatch.ts`, and fences each later step on the current device context.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `packages/client/src/browser-custody.ts`, whole.\n  - Opening: open admits only version 2 with exactly the four stores, out-of-line keys and no auto increment. It creates the layout only from old version 0, and it refuses every other layout without clearing or converting it.\n  - Reads: each row passes `readStoredCustodyRecord`. Its key, id, target digest, phase and times must equal the parsed record. A row that is present but malformed is refused and never read as absence. `getKey` separates a missing row from an undefined value. An empty history is proved by a prefix probe from `[id]` to `[id + NUL]`.\n  - Writes: `write` validates every live row before it replaces one, checks the stored bytes in the same transaction, and moves the oldest terminal records past 64 to the archive. `segment` replaces the tail from `at` and sets the length in one transaction. `segmented` reads a bounded, contiguous range.\n  - Retirement: `close`, `versionchange` and an abandoned open retire the store for good, and every later lock, read, write or open rejects. A channel message only calls observers.\n- `packages/client/src/browser-request.ts`, whole. `deliver` keeps an accepted answer only when the trusted `recorded` port proves that the scope's record holds the exact envelope. Any other result is `Lost`, so the record stays unresolved. `read` treats an unproven receipt the same way. The context check runs before and after each await, and around the builder after admission.\n- `packages/client/src/custody.ts`. `readStoredOutcome` and `readStoredCustodyRecord` admit stored structure with the wire guards. For version 2 they check signing bounds, outcome signing indexes, and that the latest signing matches the envelope. They grant no authority. `#dispatch` enters `store.exclusive`, starts delivery, and returns from the callback before awaiting the network, for both `send` and `step`.\n- `packages/client/src/browser-joining.ts`. The join slot is now `{ v: 2, seat, key }` and is written before signing. The record must be a `join` by this device's key, to the seat's membership, with this membership version's fields. An unreadable find keeps the slot. Only a successful null find under a current context clears it as unsigned. Each fetch goes through `contextFetch`, so an expired context makes no request.\n- The Counter and Lending clients, their storage, the two migrated Native callers, and the Counter tests that the deleted dispatcher owned. Counter's `client.test.ts` drops six dispatcher and journal cases and adds four custody cases. That accounts for Counting 55 against 56 on main.\n- The note, including the released-layout table, the four held lifecycle boundaries, the Voice correspondence, and the open limits.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 26d1e65c is an ancestor, and the head adds no commit of current origin main. The 46 artifacts name the head, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 26d1e65c b8d58825`, deletions included.\n- Gate, under f45b355a and act 13ea7ab7. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-14-nf5-browser-custody-full-gate-attempt3/gate.log` has SHA-256 c71b82bf…, as the request states. Its first lines name head 787f7088 and tree 11479ddd with 0 changed files. It reports Node 195, Counting 55, Plain 4760 passed and 1 skipped, Native 1134 passed and 2 skipped, and `scope-scale: omitted-by-gate`. Its last gate line is \"gate passed\". From 787f7088 to the head only this note changes.\n- Controls. The two client controls and the Voice restart control beside the gate match the note's digests. The admission control fails with `[1,0,null]` instead of `[0,0,null]`. The malformed-row control fails with \"promise resolved null instead of rejecting\". Each failure is the direct assertion for its rule.\n- Removed modules. No source, test or configuration outside `notes/` names `request-custody`, `request-attempts`, `request-dispatch` or `requestJournal`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 32 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests and no browser.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One `Custody` now holds the browser's requests, under the same record and signing rules as the CLI and MCP. The browser store adds only storage, locks and invalidation. The layout fails closed on anything it did not create, which is the right rule for a first released layout.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. A browser keeps an acceptance only with receipt proof of the exact signed request, a malformed row can never read as absence, and an expired context makes no later request, signing or slot removal. Two facts for the record:\n\n- `#dispatch` changes every custody store, not only the browser's. Each delivery now enters the store's `exclusive` section briefly. For the Node file store, `exclusive` takes the `capacity.lease` lock and throws `CustodyError({held:\"locked\"})` after `LEASE_WAIT_MS` of contention. When that happens, the record is already marked `sent` and nothing has been delivered. The existing recovery sends the same bytes again or settles them, so nothing is lost, but the CLI and the local MCP server can now report `locked` at the send step. The gate covers this path only under no contention.\n- `RETIRED_REQUEST` says \"Nothing was sent.\" For a version 1 join slot or Counter record whose phase was `sent` or `unknown`, an envelope may have left before the cutover. The room retired, so no outcome matters, but the sentence can be false. A follow-up can say \"This page sent nothing now\", or drop the sentence. Request c288c917 asks only that the page say the room retired.\n\nSimplification: the head deletes three modules, their exports and their tests, and leaves one custody path. No required change.\n\nThe note states its limits: no native IndexedDB atomicity proof beyond the real-browser witness, reload recovery is not power-loss durability, Lending's gateway fences have source review and compiler coverage only, and NF7 request 13ff61c7 still owes the hosted Counter witness. A hosted failure reopens NF-5, as the note says.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing, deployment, signing or publication. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:578b3e135a634a4920c3fccddc4f9ae32c4c1319","binding":"assigned","head":"b8d58825fed6475718761771096f6f7e8b644b8f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:179edd2276d722f749f60d7590a91b63506b7ac3\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:11ad3b377f2ff807ed5dc9be85b79c038d00acaf\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f09020c1be9c64170beb810bdada5e1349ace631","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:049f20c5be4bf9b931e2a3b17c58ee482654b6d4, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06237ac0edb5e6d93d5fe9c9f9bb841c01fbfb55, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0b524b76231732ccddc1efbc5386b8bb808edf80, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:10003fc28076f87d8d1df8b5ebe76ee60413038a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:11aac471efbda8eca15e2291a67cf5e6b0b804d3, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:179edd2276d722f